<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Maple Grove &mdash; Executive Brief</title><style>body{font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.5;}h1{font-size:16pt;color:#1e3a5f;border-bottom:2pt solid #e8a020;padding-bottom:4pt;margin-bottom:2pt;}h2{font-size:13pt;color:#1e3a5f;margin:14pt 0 4pt;border-bottom:1pt solid #edf0f4;padding-bottom:2pt;}h3{font-size:11.5pt;color:#1e3a5f;margin:11pt 0 3pt;}a{color:#1155cc;text-decoration:underline;}.banner{background:#fff4d6;border:1pt solid #e8a020;color:#7a5b00;font-size:9.5pt;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:0 0 12pt;}.sub{color:#4a5568;font-size:10pt;margin:2pt 0 4pt;}.hdr{font-size:10pt;color:#23344a;margin:1pt 0;}.hdr b{color:#1e3a5f;}.outcome{font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;color:#14532d;background:#e8f5ec;border-left:3pt solid #1a7a4a;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:8pt 0;}.bottomline{background:#eef3fa;border-left:3pt solid #1e3a5f;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:8pt 0;}ul{margin:4pt 0 8pt 0;}li{margin:2pt 0;}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:10pt;margin:6pt 0;}th,td{border:1pt solid #cdd6e0;padding:4pt 6pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;}th{background:#1e3a5f;color:#fff;font-size:9.5pt;}blockquote{margin:5pt 0 5pt 14pt;padding:3pt 0 3pt 10pt;border-left:2pt solid #cdd6e0;color:#33414f;font-style:italic;}.spk{font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;color:#1e3a5f;}.meta{color:#4a5568;font-size:9pt;border-top:1pt solid #edf0f4;padding-top:6pt;margin-top:18pt;}</style></head><body><h1>Maple Grove &mdash; Executive Brief</h1><p class="sub">Detailed segment summary &middot; Version 1 of 3 (Executive Brief)</p><div class="banner"><b>DRAFT — illustrative example.</b> Structure proposal only. Built around a fictional Westfield, IN rezoning hearing to demonstrate the format; figures are not real and are pending validation against the 10-segment research study (see proposal &sect;5). Timestamp links are illustrative.</div><div class="hdr"><b>Project:</b> Maple Grove &mdash; residential PUD subdivision</div><div class="hdr"><b>Jurisdiction / body:</b> City of Westfield, Hamilton County, IN &middot; Advisory Plan Commission</div><div class="hdr"><b>Meeting date:</b> May 19, 2026</div><div class="hdr"><b>Agenda item:</b> Docket 2605-PUD-04 &middot; Ordinance 26-15 (rezone AG-SF1 &rarr; PUD)</div><div class="hdr"><b>Segment:</b> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">[18:42]</a>&ndash;<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2490s">[41:30]</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">open video at segment start</a></div><div class="outcome">APPROVED 6&ndash;1 &mdash; favorable recommendation forwarded to City Council (June 8, 2026).</div><h2>What happened</h2><ul><li>Petitioner Arbor Homes sought to rezone ~62 acres from AG-SF1 to PUD for <b>184 single-family lots</b>. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1215s">[20:15]</a></li><li>Planning staff recommended approval subject to conditions. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">[18:42]</a></li><li>Commissioner concerns centered on traffic at 161st &amp; Oak Rd and school capacity. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1670s">[27:50]</a></li><li>Three residents spoke (2 opposed on traffic/schools, 1 in favor on housing need). <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1990s">[33:10]</a></li><li>Four conditions attached, incl. a traffic study before Council and a 20-ft tree buffer. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2285s">[38:05]</a></li></ul><h2>Vote</h2><p>6&ndash;1 favorable recommendation; lone dissent on traffic adequacy. (Roll call in V2/V3.) <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2465s">[41:05]</a></p><div class="bottomline"><b>Bottom line for MRD:</b> 184-lot Arbor Homes project clears Plan Commission with conditions and moves to Council on Jun 8 &mdash; track for the traffic-study outcome, which is the live gating risk before final approval.</div><p class="meta"><b>Sources:</b> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519">Meeting recording (YouTube)</a> &middot; <a href="#">Agenda packet (PDF)</a> &middot; <a href="#">Staff report (PDF)</a><br>Detailed agenda-item summary &mdash; generated from the meeting transcript by MRD (Municipal Resource Dashboard), scoped to this project&rsquo;s agenda item. Timestamp links open the cited moment in the source video.</p></body></html>